    "Compile soprano, alto, tenore and basso separately from notes.lyi, retaining their cross-staff notes and internal subdivisions. The explicit bar-23 cross-voice F♯ tie is one event assigned to its originating Alto voice, not a new Soprano attack. The aggregate pitch/onset set equals the published MIDI. Isolated variables avoid the anonymous child-voice reuse that places the alto’s closing D♯ in the published soprano MIDI track."
